prints["Coalfield"]={id="Coalfield",title="Coalfield",text="Coalfield, Kentucky\n\nA Taste of the Wild West\n\nFounded in the 1850s as a stop for travelers heading east, Coalfield became notorious for a series of conflicts between Sheriff Everett Holloway and Irvin Bradshaw and his gang.\nThe feud culminated with a massive shootout on the night of August 11, 1882, which ended when the Lawman's Distillery caught fire and exploded, taking many buildings with it. No sign of Everett Holloway or Irvin Bradshaw was ever found.\n\nNow you can visit the original site of Coalfield, renovated accurately. Visit our general store, have a drink in the saloons, experience life as a blacksmith, tour period cabins, and see what the Old West was really like!\n\nCome along every Saturday for a reenactment of the shootout between Holloway's lawmen and the Bradshaw gang!\n\n1. Church\n2. Greengrocer & Dry Goods\n3. El Grande Saloon\n4. Iron West Hardware\n5. Horseshoe Taphouse\n6. Miss Honey's Beauty Parlor\n7. Sheriff\n8. Rancher Chophouse\n9. Porter & Son\n10. Bank\n11. Coalfield Public House\n12. Smith & Farrier\n13. Coalfield Inn\n14. Entrance Building",locations={{x=3479,y=8267}}}
printList[#printList+1]="Coalfield"
prints["ColdWarBunker"]={id="ColdWarBunker",title="March Ridge Cold War Bunker",text="Tour a Future that didn't happen!\n\nJust off Adams Road in northern March Ridge sits a fenced area with a small shed and a radio tower.\n\nFor decades, this was the entrance to a top secret nuclear bunker, built to house Fort Knox's military leaders.\n\nBuilt four storeys underground in 1960, with thick steel doors, the bunker was made to withstand a direct nuclear hit on Fort Knox itself.\n\nSpace was limited, with beds for only forty people. It's unlikely the bunker would have survived for long without resupply.\n\nThankfully, armageddon did not arrive.\n\nThe bunker was decommissioned in 1991 and is now available for weekend tours!\n\nBook ahead on 943-555-7843.\n\nNote: Tour not suitable for the claustrophobic or young children. Bunker has not been fully checked for asbestos and some forms of poisoning. Waivers must be signed on entry.\n\n5671 Folger Street, March Ridge, Kentucky",locations={{x=9919,y=12647}}}
printList[#printList+1]="ColdWarBunker"
prints["DarkwallowGuestHouse"]={id="DarkwallowGuestHouse",title="Darkwallow Guest House",text="Serenity waits for you at Dark Wallow Lake\n\nOur guest house has 36 rooms, each with a bathroom and a TV.\n\nAfter a long day of swimming, fishing, boating or hiking, return to your private balcony and watch the sun set...\n\n... then refuel in our restaurant, and have some fun in our bar!\n\nDark Wallow Lake.\nWhat happened here belongs in the past.",locations={{x=8587,y=14531}}}
printList[#printList+1]="DarkwallowGuestHouse"
